 {:storage/durability-first
  {:kind :hand-admitted,
   :by "kimi-6",
   :date "2026-09-24",
   :source
   {:path "futon3/library/storage/durability-first.flexiarg",
    :sha256
    "1ccc6c4cd0e224d02cd4501451706fa1be65dd6f7219dbec79f97012c4684434"},
   :reading
   "F1 asks for a SQLite canon_store.db whose scope bindings persist across runs. The pattern is the zeroth invariant: writes return success only after durable storage confirms — what you save is what you get back. Schema-with-bindings is exactly the thing that must survive restart to be a store at all.",
   :scope-limit
   "Covers durability of the store and its bindings; it does not choose the schema, and it does not make any posterior consume the store."},
  :portal/first-class-query-interface
  {:kind :hand-admitted,
   :by "kimi-6",
   :date "2026-09-24",
   :source
   {:path "futon3/library/portal/first-class-query-interface.flexiarg",
    :sha256
    "a755daf83a305869a5548e29dd15f62c51b4622ba4ac1ed45fea1ee95a03ca91"},
   :reading
   "F2 asks for an in-run query over the SQLite store with incremental state-merge and most-cited-first ranking. The pattern treats query as a first-class operation over the persisted intent rather than a fixed endpoint — the reducer reads the store through a real query interface, not a one-off scan.",
   :scope-limit
   "Covers the query surface; it does not validate the ranking heuristics (most-cited-first) against any gold standard."},
  :aif/two-layer-calibration
  {:kind :hand-admitted,
   :by "kimi-6",
   :date "2026-09-24",
   :source
   {:path "futon3/library/aif/two-layer-calibration.flexiarg",
    :sha256
    "76a281cd37088f9de561ff72f8d5874180d12fe2b1103f190e57d5cc196c8366"},
   :reading
   "F4 demands the literature-lifted strategy-merge proposer be validated on held-out gold with a no-regression check. The pattern separates the two layers: internal consistency of the proposer in one layer, preregistered held-out evidence with declared metrics in a separately labelled empirical layer. A consistency pass does not substitute for the held-out packet.",
   :scope-limit
   "Covers the validation discipline; it does not build the proposer, and if the held-out gold does not exist the task stays open rather than passing on in-sample evidence."},
  :sidecar/append-only-semantic-audit
  {:kind :hand-admitted,
   :by "kimi-6",
   :date "2026-09-24",
   :source
   {:path "futon3/library/sidecar/append-only-semantic-audit.flexiarg",
    :sha256
    "20b4c6ea725c9636f768742d372d0862eb3a872bb21b42ba14724c96be892f4e"},
   :reading
   "F5 closes the loop: read store on startup, use it as prior, MAP-append, incremental REDUCE. The pattern keeps semantic writes append-only with provenance at the store boundary, so the loop's merges are inspectable and reversible instead of overwriting the prior state.",
   :scope-limit
   "Covers the append-only merge discipline of the loop; it does not prove the merged posterior is well-calibrated, and F3's per-binding posterior remains a separate task this reading does not claim."}},
